    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 the source for the generated DTOs:\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`string`/`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (request + stored/returned field).\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema's read-only block.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** entity \u2014 added a `birthDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a new `birth_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps `birthDate` DTO\u2194entity automatically by name.\n\n3. **`AgeBand.java`** (new, mapper package) \u2014 follows the `ContactPreference` precedent: returns `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`, computing whole years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` via `Period.between`, banding as MINOR (<18), ADULT (18\u201364), SENIOR (65+); returns `null` when no `birthDate` so the field is omitted.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"java(AgeBand.of(owner))\")`, so both the POST and GET responders (which call `toOwnerDto`) emit it.\n\n5. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Required because the test profile (`hsqldb`) runs with `ddl-auto=none` and relies on the explicit schema.\n\n**Why against `registrationDate`:** `AgeBand.of` reads `owner.getRegistrationDate()`, which `BuildOwner` has already resolved to the effective (supplied-or-defaulted, business-day-adjusted) date \u2014 matching the spec. The test (`birthDate=1990-01-01`, registration defaults to today ~2026 \u2192 age ~36 \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, as does the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1).\n\nNo git repository here, so nothing was committed.",
