        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `AgeBand` is a dedicated derivation helper, not logic stuffed into the `OwnerMapper` interface expression or the `Owner` entity. It mirrors the existing `ContactPreference` almost exactly: same `mapper` package, `final` class with private constructor, a single static `of(Owner)` returning an `OwnerDto.*Enum`, and the same javadoc style (\"Derives the `{field}` field produced by `{@link OwnerMapper#toOwnerDto}`\u2026\").\n- **Package placement is correct.** Helpers that return an `OwnerDto.*Enum` and serve only the mapper live in the `mapper` package (`ContactPreference`), while `model`-package helpers (`MembershipLevel`, `CustomerCode`, `OwnerIdentity`) return domain types/primitives and are shared beyond the mapper. `AgeBand` returns `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` and is used only in the mapping, so `mapper` is the natural home.\n- **Mapper wiring** follows the established `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(X.of(owner))\")` convention and sits sensibly among its siblings.\n- **Entity + schema changes** are consistent: `birthDate` placed next to `registrationDate` with a matching getter/setter, and the `birth_date DATE` column added uniformly across all four dialect schemas. OpenAPI additions (request `birthDate`, read-only `ageBand` enum) are complete and well-described.\n- Named constants `ADULT_FROM`/`SENIOR_FROM` keep the band thresholds self-documenting. No duplication, no catch-all accumulation.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural."
